## 5. Testing strategy

Documents can't be unit-tested, but they can be checked:

| Check | How |
|---|---|
| Rules are complete | For each sample record, the rules doc alone determines the outcome. Do the "stranger test" from §1 |
| Rules are consistent with the schema | Every enum/status/type in the docs exists in a `CHECK` constraint, and vice versa: `grep -o "'[A-Z_]*'" src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__initial_schema.sql \| sort -u` against the docs |
| Every requirement is traceable | Each FR/NFR names a TASKS.md task; each task in M3–M8 is covered by an FR/NFR |
| Samples are valid against the contract | Visually now; in M5.22 an integration test imports every sample |
| Mermaid diagrams render | Push the branch and view the files on GitHub |
| Links work | Click every link in the PR's rich diff view |

The real tests of this phase come later: M5.21 (one test per normalization rule ID), M5.22 (samples import as documented), M6.18 (engine reproduces `samples/README.md`), M6.19 (the invariant).

